BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Bouquets and Budgets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260210T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260210T130000
UID:a984b7e32c6c7508d3c16c27d071501d1282026_6:37:05_PM@campusgroups.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to learn about fundraising and grants for Registered Stud
 ent Organizations\, while making your own bouquet for Valentines? Join us 
 at this event where we'll share tips to get started in fundraising: from m
 aintaining your agency account\, to setting up on-campus fundraisers and a
 pplying for grants.\n\nSweet treats from Fluffy Donuts provided\, and the 
 first few organizations that attend will get a free Fundraising Starter Pa
 ck (30 sealable cellophane bags for individually wrapped items\, 30 thank 
 you stickers\, 1 plastic flyer stand\, 2 plastic tablecloths). You must be
  an active Registered Student Organization with the Center for Student Inv
 olvement in order to receive the pack! While supplies last.\n\nAll are wel
 come\, and please note that there is limited seating space due to the bouq
 uet activity.
LOCATION:Student Community Center\, Meeting Room D\, 1 Shields Ave\, Davis
 \, California 95616\, United States
URL:https://aggielife.ucdavis.edu/rsvp?id=908260
X-SOURCE:UC Davis CampusGroups
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Black Fem/me Magic Week Presents: Black Women and Activism: Explor
 ing History through Zine Making
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260210T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260210T150000
UID:751033e23499b2fe3c231e4597618fb6252026_7:12:20_PM@campusgroups.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in kicking off Black Fem/me Magic Week as we step back
  into Black history. Come for an afternoon of knowledge sharing through ma
 king zines as we discuss Black women and activism in American history.\n\n
 Free boba and food will be provided\, as well as zines. Pick up a zine for
  you and a friend\, too!\n\nDate: Tue. Feb. 10th\nTime: 2-3pm\nLocation: W
 RRC Library\n\n[Colorful text and title describe a zine-making event about
  Black women and activism in American history\, with free food\, boba and 
 zines. Flyer includes colorful shapes and black-and-white photos of Audre 
 Lorde and other Black women activists . Logos for the UC Davis Women’s R
 esources and Research Center and Black Fem/me Magic Week on bottom of the 
 flyer.]
URL:https://aggielife.ucdavis.edu/rsvp?id=908328
X-SOURCE:UC Davis CampusGroups
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Student Life Impact Awards Info Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260210T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260210T163000
UID:a8648b0b7e205dfd43d3912c71a9b9f81222026_4:10:02_PM@campusgroups.com
DESCRIPTION:Have questions about the Student Life Impact Awards? Want to a
 pply but don't know where to start? \n\nCome to the Student Life Impact A
 ward Info Sessions! We will go over the rubrics and general considerations
  for the applications\, troubleshooting any technical difficulties\, help 
 you double check your eligibility\, and answer frequently asked questions.
  All awards discussed during the info session are open to all to apply.\n\
 nThe awards we will be discussing: \nIndividual Student Awards\nAdams Awa
 rd for Leadership in a Student Organization ($500)\nCivic Engagement Award
 s ($500 each)\nFirst Year Student\nUndergraduate Student\nGraduate Student
 \nMargarita Robinson Student Leadership Award ($500)\nSusan F. Regan Pryta
 nean Award ($2\,000 each)\nStudent Promoting Advocacy and Redefining Commu
 nity Award ($500)\nCommencement Awards (Must be graduating by the end of S
 ummer Session)\nMary Jeanne Gilhooly Award ($1\,000)\nSocial Justice and I
 nclusion Award ($1\,000)\nVeloyce Glenn Winslow Jr. Award ($1\,000)\nRegis
 tered Student Organization Awards\nCivic Engagement Award ($1\,000)\nBuild
 ing Career Pathways Award ($200)\nThe EXperiential Learning (EXL) Award ($
 200)\nTrailblazing Innovators Award ($200)\n\nMeeting Link: https://ucdavi
 s.zoom.us/j/6617840817?pwd=VkMrNy8rTVdKWm5kcS9WOStIRkpKZz09
LOCATION:Online Event
URL:https://aggielife.ucdavis.edu/rsvp?id=908210
X-SOURCE:UC Davis CampusGroups
END:VEVENT
