 asing the historical and contemporary significance of fashion across cultu
 res\, highlighting how style reflects identity\, heritage\, and creative e
 xpression.\n\nAll students are welcome to show off their own designs and c
 ontemporary interpretations\, traditional garments\, cultural textiles and
  silhouettes\, or just to watch the show!\n\n📅Thursday\, February 19th\
 n⏰5:00pm-6:15pm\n📍Wyatt Pavilion Theatre\n\n🌟Students must RSVP fo
 r as we have limited capacity capped at 20 participants and 60 attendees.\
 n\nRSVP in our link in bio!\n\nAlt Text for Flyer:\n\nFlyer with a white b
 ackground featuring individuals dressed in various culturally relevant sty
 les with a purple duotone effect. Text reads: “Threads of Tradition: Cel
 ebrating Culture on the Runway. THUR. February 19TH | 5:00PM-6:15PM | Wyat
 t Pavilion Theatre. Featuring contemporary interpretations\, cultural text
 iles and silhouettes\, student designs\, traditional garments\, and light 
 refreshments!
