DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260221T190000
UID:d2251d70c5f68bc7b9075b2fe696be9f292026_7:25:32_PM@campusgroups.com
DESCRIPTION:The Hult Prize at UC Davis OnCampus Competition is the officia
 l qualifying round of the Hult Prize\, a global social entrepreneurship co
 mpetition challenging students to build for-profit ventures that address p
 ressing global issues aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Developm
 ent Goals.\n\nStudent teams will pitch their startup ideas in front of a p
 anel of judges\, delivering a 4-minute pitch followed by a 4-minute Q&A. J
 udges will evaluate teams based on team strength\, idea quality\, social i
 mpact\, and business viability.\n\nThe top three teams from this OnCampus 
 Competition can advance to the next stage of the Hult Prize pathway and be
 come eligible to compete at national competition.
URL:https://aggielife.ucdavis.edu/rsvp?id=908343
X-SOURCE:UC Davis CampusGroups
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cultural Event
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260221T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260221T213000
UID:76c714ecbedc1b48340726e337ad75781132026_3:24:59_PM@campusgroups.com
DESCRIPTION:This event is centered around a vibrant series of performances
  that highlight the rich traditions and culture of the Hmong people. It wi
 ll help students at UC Davis gain a deeper understanding of the Hmong heri
 tage. It will provide Hmong students a space where they can see their cult
 ure represented\, affirmed and celebrated\, thereby fostering a sense of b
 elonging and cultural pride. By inviting not only Hmong students but also 
 non-Hmong peers\, we create a shared experience of learning and appreciati
 on. The Hmong cultural practices\, whether music\, dance\, fashion\, or fo
 od all carry stories of migration\, resilience\, and identity.
URL:https://aggielife.ucdavis.edu/rsvp?id=908021
X-SOURCE:UC Davis CampusGroups
END:VEVENT
