BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aggie Resilience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260228T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260228T170000
UID:aad96700729e674bed4fcb8ba2aa213d1152026_5:26:34_PM@campusgroups.com
DESCRIPTION:Aggie Resilience is a multi-institutional professional develop
 ment and community-building event that brings together graduate students a
 nd mentors affiliated with the Promised Engineering Institute (PEI)\, UC D
 avis\, UC Irvine\, Stanford\, and UMBC\, as well as members of the Nationa
 l Organization for the Professional Advancement of Black Chemists and Chem
 ical Engineers (NOBCChE)\, the Society of Water and Environmental Graduate
  Students\, and other campus and professional partners. The event is open 
 to students and scholars who are seeking support\, mentorship\, and empowe
 rment through shared experiences. The colloquium centers on resilience-bui
 lding for historically marginalized students through a full-day program th
 at includes keynote and panel discussions (featuring students\, postdoctor
 al researchers\, and faculty)\, professional development workshops\, mento
 rship and networking opportunities\, testimonials\, and moments of celebra
 tion recognizing academic and professional accomplishments.
LOCATION:1330 Walker Hall\, 1 Shields Ave\, Davis\, California 95616\, Uni
 ted States
URL:https://aggielife.ucdavis.edu/rsvp?id=908151
X-SOURCE:UC Davis CampusGroups
END:VEVENT
